	<http://schema.org/name> "Insecure Third-Party Libraries" ;
	<http://schema.org/description> "Third-party libraries incorporated into mobile apps could contain malicious behavior, privacy-invasive behavior, or exploitable vulnerabilities. An adversary could deliberately insert malicious behavior or could exploit inadvertent vulnerabilities.  For example, Ryan Welton of NowSecure identified exploitable remote code execution vulnerabilities in a third-party advertisement library (Citation: NowSecure-RemoteCode). Grace et al. identified security issues in mobile advertisement libraries (Citation: Grace-Advertisement).  Platforms: Android, iOS" ;
	<http://w3id.org/sepses/vocab/ref/attack#platform> "Android" , "iOS" ;
	<http://schema.org/dateModified> "2018-01-17T12:56:55.080Z" ;
